  "_comment": "Per-faction unit and ship names, the stat trade each renaming carries, and the two small bonuses every realm has. Owner-specified in 0.20.0; the names and the figures are Claude's and are [GEN]. Names are period-appropriate to 1300-1500 and may repeat across factions on purpose — a Carrack served half of Europe. Deltas are added to the base figure in data/units.json, so retuning a base unit carries through to every faction. Only combat and marching stats may vary: hp, damage and strategicSpeed. Cost, size, upkeep and build time are deliberately identical everywhere, so a faction is never richer or more populous for its roster, only different on the field.",
  "_bonusKinds": "economy: gold | wood | iron | stone (permille of that income) or growth (whole people per settlement per month). military: hp | damage | march (permille, applied to every unit the realm fields).",

